package app_test

// Test harness for internal/app (WP-32).
//
// The harness wires the services exactly as cmd/cuisle would: storetest DB, fixed clock, recording Emitter, in-memory
// Keyring, the real jiratest fake over jiratest.DefaultFixture (plus one kanban board, see buildFixture), the real
// Jira adapter registered through source.Register, a real sync.Orchestrator and a real sink.Dispatcher.
//
// SPEC-NOTE: (fixture) jiratest.DefaultFixture is generated by cmd/fixturegen (design/reference/sample-data.json). It
// is an empty placeholder until that work package lands, so newTestApp fails with a clear message when it is empty.
// Expected values are DERIVED from the parsed fixture (first scrum board, an in-sprint active issue, ...) rather than
// hard-coded, so the tests keep working when the fixture content changes. Two things are appended to the parsed
// fixture because the sample has no such data: a kanban project/board ("OPSX") and an unassigned-to-anything user
// ("Zed Quinn"), which the kanban, add-speaker and search tests need.
//
// SPEC-NOTE: (sink wiring gap) sink.BuildFunc is documented as "supplied by the app" and sink.DispatcherOptions.Notify
// is documented as "becomes sink:delivered / sink:failed", but internal/app exports neither a BuildFunc constructor
// nor a Notify adapter. The harness therefore builds the BuildFunc itself (StandupService.View + ConfigService.Get ->
// export.Build/Encode, late-bound through ta.Svc) and leaves Notify nil. The tests do not assert sink:delivered or
// sink:failed events, because the only producer would be code in this harness. Suggested contract addition:
// `func NewSinkBuild(d *Deps) sink.BuildFunc` and `func SinkNotifier(e syncpkg.Emitter) func(sink.Event)` in
// internal/app, used by both cmd/cuisle and these tests.
//
// SPEC-NOTE: (offline simulation) "offline" is simulated with a toggleable http.RoundTripper installed as both
// Deps.HTTP and Deps.SourceOpts.HTTP that fails with a DNS error (jira-sync.md section 3: "DNS failure / no route"
// maps to apperr offline, no retry loop). The transport also counts every attempted round trip, so "no network" is
// asserted both against the fake's request log AND against attempted calls.

